            <ArticleTitle>Effect on survival of previous angina pectoris after acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1534-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although the present study revealed that previous angina improved in-hospital outcome, no further benefit was observed once the patients left the hospital. The worse long-term prognosis was associated with multi-vessel coronary disease in patients with previous angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
